  "lessons": "- **Indigenous, Canadian regional, and community life:** Strongly favored: First Nations advocacy, reconciliation, land stewardship, and substantive community news from BC interior and Saskatchewan (civic affairs, housing, hospice planning, local fire bans). Sports recaps, routine event listings, and empty local portal pages are rejected.\n- **Environmental framing:** Accepted when the angle is solutions, protection, policy stakes, or industry pivots, and when stakes are clear (water scarcity, microplastics, persistent chemicals). Pure disaster or weather coverage (smoke, heat, drought headlines) is mostly rejected.\n- **EV and automotive:** Accepted for automaker strategy, corporate turnarounds, and battery breakthroughs. Rejected for ownership decline, sales drops, model cancellations, spec-sheet reviews, and car listicles.\n- **Science & nature discovery:** Strongly favored: surprising natural phenomena, animal and evolutionary biology, astronomy, geoscience, critical minerals, and novel research with real-world implications. Wellness pseudoscience and symptom-driven health advice are rejected; environmentally or neurologically grounded health research can land.\n- **AI & tech policy and risk:** Accepted for security vulnerabilities, attacks on AI systems, substantive legal rulings, expert warnings about societal impact, and critiques of bubbles or overreach. Product launches, model hype, feature updates, funding deals, and appointments are rejected.\n- **Practical tech:** Privacy and security how-tos are valued; deals, roundups, sales, benchmarks, device refreshes, and gift guides are rejected. Simple consumer tips and leak coverage are rejected unless they reveal a substantive product shift.\n- **General news",
